ent":"scanning calorimeter (DSC 111 purchased from Setaram Co.)","method":"differential thermal analyses","page":3,"quote":"Each cylindrical cell--laboratory and refere n c e - - i s surrounded by a thermal fluxmeter and located into a metallic block, the temperature of which can be linearly programmed. The cell is a gas-tight silica (or Pyrex or stainless steel) tube 6 mm in diameter and 20 mm in length. The heating (or cooling) rate varies from 2 K. mn-1 to 4 K. mn -]. We estimated the maximum experimental error on the temperature at ---0.5 K.","quote_chars_original":657,"quote_clipped":true,"second_reader_agrees":false,"stated_uncertainty":"---0.5 K","type":"measurement"},{"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-RLLLVBQPJS","label":"Ag + Au + Ge alloys","page":3,"quote":"All the samples of Ag + Au + Ge alloys were previously synthesized. Stoichiometric amounts of gold, silver, and germanium were introduced into a quartz cell and sealed under purified argon atmosphere. The total mass of each sample was about 500 mg. These alloys were prepared and homogenized in the liquid state into a separate furnace during many heating-cooling cycles; then they were introduced into the laboratory crucible for thermal analysis.","second_reader_agrees":true,"starting_materials":"gold, silver, and germanium","synthesis":"Stoichiometric amounts of gold, silver, and germanium were introduced into a quartz cell and sealed under purified argon atmosphere. The total mass of each sample was about 500 mg. These alloys were prepared and homogenized in the liquid state into a separate furnace during many heating-cooling cycles; then they were introduced into the laboratory crucible for thermal analysis.","type":"sample"}],"paper":"doi:10.1007/bf02649254","reader_tier":"preliminary_flash","readers":["gemini-3.8-flash / exp-context-v2.1-quote","claude-opus-5.5 / exp-context-v2.1-quote (claude broker)"],"section_basis":"methods_heading"}},"elements":["AG","AU"],"licence":"CC BY 4.0 (ORCHID data; 